Neko Project II kai is an emulator of the NEC PC-9801 series of Japanese
personal computers, based on Neko Project II. This port builds its libretro
core, for use with RetroArch and other libretro frontends.

It supports floppy disk images (.hdm, .fdi, .d88 and others) and hard disk
images (.hdi, .nhd, .thd). CD-ROM images (.cue) can be loaded through a
.cmd file.
